-- title:
--   The augmented configuration graph is generated by local moves that depend only on the scanned symbol
-- statement:
--   Let $\Sigma$ be an alphabet and let $A=(Q,q_0,F,\delta)$ be a two-way nondeterministic automaton over $\Sigma$: $Q$ is an arbitrary set of states, $q_0\in Q$ is the initial state, $F\subseteq Q$ is the set of accepting states, and $\delta$ assigns to every state $q$ and every tape symbol $b\in\{\vdash,\dashv\}\sqcup\Sigma$ a set $\delta(q,b)\subseteq Q\times\{L,S,R\}$ of pairs (next state, head move). A word $w=a_1\cdots a_n\in\Sigma^*$ is written on the tape positions $0,1,\dots,n+1$ as $\vdash a_1\cdots a_n\dashv$, and $b_i$ denotes the symbol at position $i$. A configuration is a pair $(q,i)$ with $q\in Q$ and $0\le i\le n+1$, and $(q,i)\to(q',j)$ is a step if $(q',\mu)\in\delta(q,b_i)$ and $j=i+\Delta(\mu)$, where $\Delta(L)=-1$, $\Delta(S)=0$, $\Delta(R)=1$; a move that would leave the tape is not a step. The language $\mathcal{L}(A)$ is the set of words $w$ for which some configuration with an accepting state is reachable from $(q_0,0)$ by finitely many steps, possibly none; $\to^{*}$ denotes this reachability.
--
--   Fix a word $w=a_1\cdots a_n$. The augmented configuration graph of $A$ on $w$ uses a fresh state $f\notin Q$ and one extra position $n+2$ to the right of $\dashv$. Its vertices are the pairs $(s,i)$ with $s\in Q\sqcup\{f\}$ and $0\le i\le n+2$, and its edges $c\rightsquigarrow d$ are of three kinds:
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   &(q,i)\rightsquigarrow(q',j) && \text{whenever } (q,i)\to(q',j) \text{ is a step of } A \text{ on } w,\\
--   &(q,i)\rightsquigarrow(f,i) && \text{whenever } q\in F \text{ and } 0\le i\le n+1,\\
--   &(f,i)\rightsquigarrow(f,i+1) && \text{for } 0\le i\le n+1 .
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   Configurations of $A$ are embedded by $\iota(q,i)=(q,i)$, and $\rightsquigarrow^{*}$ denotes reachability by zero or more edges.
--
--   For a tape symbol $b\in\{\vdash,\dashv\}\sqcup\Sigma$ and a move $\mu\in\{L,S,R\}$, let $T_b(\mu)$ be the following relation on $Q\sqcup\{f\}$: for $q,r\in Q$,
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   (q,r)\in T_b(\mu)&\iff (r,\mu)\in\delta(q,b),\ \text{and}\ \mu\neq L\ \text{if}\ b=\vdash,\ \text{and}\ \mu\neq R\ \text{if}\ b=\dashv,\\
--   (q,f)\in T_b(\mu)&\iff q\in F\ \text{and}\ \mu=S,\\
--   (f,f)\in T_b(\mu)&\iff \mu=R,
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--   and $(f,r)\notin T_b(\mu)$ for all $r\in Q$. Then for all vertices $(s,i)$ and $(t,j)$ of the augmented graph,
--   $$
--   (s,i)\rightsquigarrow(t,j)\iff i\le n+1\ \text{ and there is }\mu\in\{L,S,R\}\text{ with }(s,t)\in T_{b_i}(\mu)\ \text{and}\ j=i+\Delta(\mu).
--   $$
--
--   So the augmented graph is the configuration graph of a machine on the states $Q\sqcup\{f\}$ whose possible moves depend only on the scanned symbol; position $n+2$ carries no symbol and has no outgoing edges. The explicit endmarker conditions are part of the local rule because the augmented tape does have a position to the right of $\dashv$. This locality is what allows the augmented graph to be identified with the step graph of a chain of cells $\vdash,a_1,\dots,a_n,\dashv$ followed by a terminal position, and hence with a product of boundary diagrams.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `TwoNFA Sigma Q` has fields `initial`, `accepting` and `transition`; tape symbols are `Fin 2 ⊕ Sigma` with `Sum.inl 0` and `Sum.inl 1` the endmarkers $\vdash$ and $\dashv$ (read by `tapeSymbol w`), the moves $L,S,R$ are `0, 1, 2 : Fin 3` with displacement `move.val - 1` computed in the integers, configurations are `Q × Fin (w.length + 2)`, the step relation is `A.step w`, and reachability is `relStar`, the reflexive–transitive closure. The fresh state is `none : Option Q`, the states of $Q$ appear as `some q`, and augmented positions are `Fin (w.length + 3)`; $\iota$ is `augmentConfig`, which applies `some` to the state and `Fin.castSucc` to the position, and the edge relation $\rightsquigarrow$ is `A.augmentedStep w`. The relation $T_b(\mu)$ is `A.augmentedMove b move` on `Option Q`. The condition $i\le n+1$ is stated as the existence of `p : Fin (w.length + 2)` with `c.2 = p.castSucc`, the symbol is `tapeSymbol w p`, and the displacement equation is stated in the integers.
